Finding: {"title":"routes-ai-curriculum-builder.ts POST /ai-curriculum/build stores the full request body via `as never` with only 3 fields validated","severity":"LOW","area":"Input validation","files":["src/server/routes/routes-ai-curriculum-builder.ts"],"detail":"Line 603-617: the handler validates only `programType`, `regulatoryFramework`, `locationId` are present, then inserts the entire parsed JSON body directly into `curriculumBuildJobs.builderParams` via `body as never` (line 630) — bypassing TypeScript's structural checking entirely. Nested fields like `targetHours.total/dual/solo/sim/ground`, `stageCount`, `contentCustomization`, etc. are never validated for type or range (e.g. `stageCount` could be `0`, negative, or a string; `targetHours` could be missing entirely, which would then produce `NaN`/`undefined` deep inside `buildCurriculumPrompt`, e.g. line 479's template interpolation).","impact":"A malformed request that passes the 3-field check but has garbage/missing nested fields still enqueues a DB row and an Inngest job, wasting a build slot and a Claude API call before failing deep inside prompt construction or parsing — rather than being rejected cleanly at the API boundary.","recommendation":"Add a zod (or similar) schema validating BuilderParams shape (or at minimum stageCount > 0 and targetHours.* are positive numbers) before the DB insert, matching the level of validation the analyzer/export routes apply to their inputs (title/stages presence checks).","confidence":"low"}
confirmed=true only if the defect genuinely exists. If misread → verdict="false-positive". If real but wrong severity → set correctedSeverity. If real but underspecified → verdict="needs-detail" (kept). Return JSON per the schema.

